  "source": "[G1 ::= (X1, *_1, e1) \\.group.direct.product./ G2 ::= (X2, *_2, e2)]\nDefines: G3 ::= (X3, *_3, e3) is \\group\nwhen: G1, G2 is \\group\nexpresses:\n. X3 := {(x1, x2) : x1 \"in\" X1; x2 \"in\" X2}\n. (a1_, a2_) *_3 (b1_, b2_) := (a1_ *_1 b1_, a2_ *_2 b2_)\n. e3 := (e1, e2)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"direct product of groups $G1?$ and $G2?$\"\n. written: \"G1? \\times G2?\"\n. description: \"The direct product $G_1 \\times G_2$ has as elements the ordered\n                pairs $(x_1, x_2)$ with $x_i \\in G_i$, and multiplies them\n                coordinatewise. Its identity is the pair of identities, and it\n                is itself a group.\"\nId: \"3a354c63-fc8c-4873-9751-62ecc651a5a9\"",
